# Citation metadata for the tool, which GitHub renders as "Cite this
# repository". Deliberately says nothing about the dataset's own citation: this
# software and the Flickr8k copy it reads are separate artifacts with separate
# terms, and the README's Data provenance section is where that copy is
# described.
#
# No `version` or `date-released` field, because there is no tagged release to
# name yet. Both belong here the day one exists.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this tool in work you publish, please cite it. The Flickr8k copy it
  explores carries its own terms and its own citation; see the Data provenance
  section of the README.
title: CV Dataset Explorer
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Aiman
    family-names: Younis
    alias: aimanyounises1
repository-code: https://github.com/aimanyounises1/cv-dataset-explorer
abstract: >-
  A local workspace for exploring, auditing, comparing and curating the Flickr8k
  image-caption dataset. Keyword, semantic, hybrid, image and region search over
  SigLIP 2 embeddings with a hubness-corrected ranking; an embedding map;
  caption-consistency, difficulty, near-duplicate and split-leakage audits;
  optional local detection and segmentation whose output stays a proposal until a
  reviewer accepts it; and reproducible album exports with provenance manifests.
  React, FastAPI and SQLite, with no cloud service, hosted search, external
  vector database or paid API on the request path.
keywords:
  - computer-vision
  - image-captioning
  - flickr8k
  - multimodal-retrieval
  - siglip
  - dataset-curation
  - data-centric-ai
  - fastapi
  - react
